@startuml Weather_Forecasts_System_Design

title Weather Forecasts System - System Design (Service Architecture)

skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam linetype ortho
skinparam nodesep 110
skinparam ranksep 90
skinparam note {
  BackgroundColor #FFFDE7
  BorderColor #AAAAAA
}

actor "End User" as User

node "Authentication Service\n<<Appwrite Authentication>>" as Auth

node "Frontend Service\n<<Web / Mobile Client>>" as Frontend

node "User Actions Server\n----\nProfile, City/Service Selection,\nSearch, Rate, Analytics\n& Aggregation API\n+ Analytics Report Worker\n(in-process background timer)" as UserServer

database "Database Service" as DB

node "Scheduler Server\n----\nPolling & Notification Dispatch" as Scheduler

cloud "External City API" as CityAPI

cloud "Partner Forecasting\nServices" as PartnerAPIs

cloud "Email Provider\n(Analytics Report Delivery)" as AnalyticsEmail

cloud "Notification Providers\n(Email / SMS / Push)" as NotifyProviders

' --- Relationships ---
User -down-> Frontend : HTTPS

Frontend -up-> Auth : Appwrite Web SDK\n(UC1, UC13, UC14)
Frontend -right-> UserServer : REST/HTTPS\n(Bearer Appwrite JWT)
Frontend -down-> CityAPI : search cities\n(UC4, no auth, stateless)

UserServer -up-> Auth : verify JWT (Server SDK);\nfetch single user's email (UC8 delivery)
UserServer -down-> DB : upsert user_id (JIT);\nread/write app data;\npoll queued analytics reports
UserServer -right-> AnalyticsEmail : email analytics report\nas PDF attachment (UC8)

Scheduler -up-> Auth : batch-fetch emails\n(users.list, <= 100 ids/call)
Scheduler -down-> DB : read subscriptions,\nwrite forecasts
Scheduler -right-> PartnerAPIs : poll forecasts
Scheduler -right-> NotifyProviders : dispatch warnings

' --- Notes ---
note top of Auth
  Sole source of truth for accounts
  (credentials, sessions, name,
  email) - never copied into the app
  DB. Holds long-lived sessions (kept
  client-side by the Web SDK); the
  Frontend mints a short-lived JWT
  (~15 min) from the session for each
  UserServer call. Sessions revocable
  server-side. Full token lifecycle:
  see UC1/UC2 sequence diagrams.
end note

note left of Frontend
  Client-only use cases (no backend
  call at all): UC1 sign-in/sign-up/
  password-reset + session restore,
  UC13 account changes, UC14 logout
  (Option A - deletes this device's
  session only, other sessions
  unaffected).

  Route guard (UC1 A4): every page
  except the login form requires a
  valid session, re-checked on every
  navigation - not just at app launch.
  No session -> redirect to login.
end note

note bottom of CityAPI
  UC4 city search: called directly by
  the Frontend, no auth needed (stateless
  lookup). On timeout/unavailability,
  Frontend falls back to cached city
  data via the User Actions Server
  (see UC4 E1/A4).
end note

note right of UserServer
  Implements UC2-UC8, UC10 and UC12:
  Profile (JIT provisioning + CitySite
  check on first authenticated call
  after login - Frontend redirects
  based on the response), Edit
  Selections, Select Cities/Services,
  Search Forecast, Rate Forecasting
  Service, Request Analytics, View
  Aggregated Forecast, Calculate
  Aggregates.

  Request Analytics (UC8) is async:
  the API queues the request and
  returns 202; the in-process
  Analytics Report Worker polls the
  DB (~5s), computes per-city forecast
  statistics, renders a PDF and emails
  it, retrying delivery until it
  succeeds. UC9 (on-demand download
  with a format choice) is not yet
  implemented.
end note

note bottom of DB
  Single shared datastore (see ER
  diagram): Users(user_id, created_at
  - JIT-provisioned, no account
  fields), Cities, Services, Forecasts,
  Ratings, Notifications,
  AnalyticsReports (one row per
  requested service, sharing a
  batch_id) + AnalyticsReportCityMetric
  (per-city computed statistics).
  No account data stored here.
end note

note bottom of Scheduler
  Implements UC11 (Poll Forecasts and
  Notify Users). Runs independently
  of user requests on a fixed
  schedule. Batch-fetches recipient
  emails from Auth once per cycle;
  retries a failed batch with backoff
  before excluding those users for
  this cycle (see UC11 A8).
end note

@enduml
